[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jijf","created_at":"2026-10-31T18:11:00Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eCurious how this holds up once it hits real workloads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"arcwrightai","username":"arcwrightai","twitter_username":null,"github_username":null,"user_id":4191471,"website_url":"https://arcwrightai.com/","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F4191471%2F3e5336ee-847a-4ade-800a-3def717f14c7.png","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F4191471%2F3e5336ee-847a-4ade-800a-3def717f14c7.png"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jikb","created_at":"2026-10-31T18:41:09Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eIt already is real workloads: both records are live crawls of 23,190 public MCP servers, read the same day by two independent crawlers, and 99.1% of 318,389 tool definitions matched byte for byte. The differences came from how servers were read (pagination, protocol version, launch environment), not from the hashing. The data and scripts are public if you want to rerun it: \u003ca href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/interop-digests-2026-10-31/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"\u003ehistor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/in...\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[]}]},{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jkpf","created_at":"2026-11-01T15:43:55Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eByte-identical tool definitions are a cost detail, not only a correctness one. The list sits at the top of the prompt, so a changed byte there, a reordered entry or a timestamp in a description, breaks the prompt cache from that point on. Tokenade exists to cut token use in agent sessions, so cache misses are on my list.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Paul Irolla","username":"paul_irolla_6b5ae261d0224","twitter_username":null,"github_username":"pi-infected","user_id":2183047,"website_url":"https://github.com/pi-infected/tokenade","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2183047%2Fc0c55e95-e0dd-4375-8123-478cede020d8.png","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2183047%2Fc0c55e95-e0dd-4375-8123-478cede020d8.png"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jl0j","created_at":"2026-11-01T16:05:31Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eAgreed, and HISTOR's records put a number on it. In the week of 25 October to 1 November it recorded 10,712 changes to the tool lists of 4,491 MCP servers. 465 of them changed nothing but a date, a timestamp or a version string. 27 servers alone stamped dates or times into their definitions 331 times, almost twice a day each: every one of those is a cache miss with no change in meaning. More broadly, 218 servers changed their list at least seven times that week, a third of all changes. Reordering isn't counted, since HISTOR's digest sorts tools and keys, so the real number of cache-breaking edits is higher.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIf Tokenade wants to flag such servers before a session starts, the per-server change history is public: \u003ca href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/changes\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"\u003ehistor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/changes\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[]}]},{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jl5h","created_at":"2026-11-01T18:15:28Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mentioned-user\" href=\"https://dev.to/alexar76\"\u003e@alexar76\u003c/a\u003e Agreed. Most of those misses start on the server side: a list that sorts itself and keeps timestamps out of its descriptions cannot break the cache. I haven't checked HISTOR's totals, so I won't repeat them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Paul Irolla","username":"paul_irolla_6b5ae261d0224","twitter_username":null,"github_username":"pi-infected","user_id":2183047,"website_url":"https://github.com/pi-infected/tokenade","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2183047%2Fc0c55e95-e0dd-4375-8123-478cede020d8.png","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2183047%2Fc0c55e95-e0dd-4375-8123-478cede020d8.png"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jl84","created_at":"2026-11-01T19:04:23Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eGood call not repeating them, because two of my numbers above were wrong. 331 changes, not 465, moved only a date or a timestamp. The other 134 changed a decimal number, and about 126 of those turn out to be prices in tool descriptions, which is a real change for anyone paying per call. The 331 aren’t spread evenly either: one server made 237 of them by writing the time it last read its own feed into a description, and the other 26 servers made 94. Your point stands; the noise is smaller and more concentrated than I wrote.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[]}]}]